XXXX-XX-XX: version 0.3.2
    - Report when a device is not an optical drive
    - Fallback to read CD-DA as any sector type when a drive refuses the CD-DA form
    - Narrow a medium error down to the blocks that do not read
    - Tell every consumer of a drive that its disc changed
    - Record blocks as unreadable only when the disc is to blame
    - Give START STOP UNIT without IMMED the time of a spin-up
    - Merge the unreadable ranges that touch
    - Add a block read for read-ahead, giving up at the first failure
    - Wait for the operations in flight before tearing a device down
    - Let the abort check end the wait for a drive to become ready
    - Pad command blocks to 12 bytes on ATAPI-subclass interfaces
    - Accept a status sent in place of the data, or behind an empty packet
    - Read sense data by its response code, and tell more of it apart
    - Do not take a logical unit with no device connected for the drive

2026-11-05: version 0.3.1
    - Move the public headers to include/
    - Split scsi.c into scsi.c, ready.c, read.c and medium.c
    - Remember the unreadable and refused blocks per device
    - Report the reason why no disc was identified
    - Optimizations

2026-10-28: version 0.3
